    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test run \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; the other two files are the abstract base and support). \n\nThe change is complete. Here's what I implemented so that `namesakeCount` = the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName and lastName, case-insensitively:\n\n1. **`CountOwnerNamesakes`** (new function class) \u2014 a create-pipeline step that reads the built `Owner`, counts existing owners in `OwnerRepository.findAll()` matching first+last name case-insensitively, and stamps the result via `owner.setNamesakeCount(count)`. It runs before `SaveOwner`, so the new owner isn't yet persisted and therefore isn't counted.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `namesakes` step between `assignCode` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the other create steps.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added the `namesakeCount` (`@Column(name = \"namesake_count\")`) field with getter/setter. It's `Integer` so pre-existing rows with a NULL column load cleanly.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `namesakeCount` read-only `int32` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically onto the GET response.\n\n5. **Schema/data SQL** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to all four `schema.sql` variants (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) and appended the extra `NULL` to the positional owner seed inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the DB the tests use; h2/postgres use column-list inserts and were unaffected).\n\nThe `coreCountsNamesakes` acceptance test \u2014 which creates two same-named owners and expects the second's `namesakeCount` to be `1` \u2014 now passes, as does the full suite.",
